  "description": "What: CE-4693 BL-S3 (docs/designs/engineering/DESIGN_Bridge_Laying.md \u00a712, BL-18) - on basic-desert a RIVER 12 m wide (y 60-72). At 2 s 'Engineer' (an assault bridge layer, TKB 118) lays its bridge from (80, 50) to (80, 82) (300 s at the bank). When the bridge is Open the rule 'Bridge laid' orders it to RecoverBridge (no bridge named: the nearest of the type it carries) and arms 'Bridge recovered'. It drives to the nearer deck end and takes the span back (600 s) through the network destroy - never a demolition. When no assault bridge is left, 'Bridge recovered' orders 'Tank' (an M1 at (60, 20)) to (80, 110) on the far bank. Judge: 'Bridge laid' and 'Bridge recovered' are Achieved; the engineer carries its span again (Count 1, no order); the river is a barrier again: the tank, ordered across, never reaches the far bank. Fail: the bridge stays, the span is not back on board, or the tank crosses. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh bl-recover"
